@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Public policy enforcement — rejected writes and hidden legacy routes
hide footbox
autonumber
actor "HTTP caller\nnot a public UI editing control" as Caller
participant "public_workspace()\npublic_access.py middleware" as Boundary
participant "state : PublicAccessState" as State
participant "rate_limits.throttle()" as Limiter
activate Caller
Caller -> Boundary : POST/PATCH/DELETE Collection or recordings;\nPUT /api/analyzer/grammar
activate Boundary
Boundary --> Caller : 403 public workspace is read-only
deactivate Boundary
Caller -> Boundary : GET /api/auth/* or /api/workspace/*;\nrequest coursework/import/backup/history/restore
activate Boundary
Boundary --> Caller : 404 API endpoint not found
deactivate Boundary
Caller -> Boundary : POST allowed analysis/lookup path\nwith wrong Origin or invalid/missing CSRF
activate Boundary
Boundary --> Caller : 403 request-origin/token error
deactivate Boundary
Caller -> Boundary : POST allowed path with valid Origin + CSRF\nbut exhausted 120-request/60-second IP window
activate Boundary
Boundary -> State : limit(client address)
activate State
State -> Limiter : throttle(public limits DB, hashed IP, 120, 60)
activate Limiter
Limiter --> State : RateLimitExceeded(retry_after)
deactivate Limiter
State --> Boundary : propagate RateLimitExceeded
deactivate State
Boundary --> Caller : 429 + Retry-After
deactivate Boundary
deactivate Caller
legend bottom
  Allowed POST paths: /api/analyze, /api/analyzer/analyze, /api/analyzer/tests, /api/readings/lookup.
  Read-only-resource path checks distinguish forbidden writes (403) from absent legacy endpoints (404).
  These failures dispatch no domain mutation. PublicWorkspaceStore also rejects forbidden writes/imports.
  This sequence depicts separate requests; every call/reply and activation is independently balanced.
endlegend
@enduml
